					<description><![CDATA[<p>As enterprises scale, they often run into problems in manual supply-chain spend management and financial leakage. Freehand raises $75 million to put AI agents in supply chains to solve this</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/freehand-raises-75-million-ai-agents-supply-chain/" data-wpel-link="internal">Freehand Raises $75 Million as AI Agents Take Up Meta and Unilever’s Supply Chains</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">As enterprises scale, they often run into problems in manual supply-chain spend management and financial leakage. Freehand </span><a href="https://x.com/freehand_ai/status/2082510919960281594" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">raises $75 million</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> to put AI agents in supply chains to solve this problem. The round was co-led by Battery Ventures and NewRoad Capital Partners.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">PSP Growth, the firm chaired by former US Commerce Secretary Penny Pritzker and Nexus Venture Partners also joined the round. Nitin Jayakrishnan, Freehand’s co-founder and CEO says that the funding is the beginning of true autonomy in the enterprise. </span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Why Enterprises Are Paying Attention</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">According to the Bureau of Economic </span><a href="https://www.bea.gov/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">Analysis</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">, American businesses spend more than $20 trillion every year on goods, logistics, technology and services. Freehand believes that model is becoming too expensive to maintain. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company estimates businesses spend billions on software while spending far more on manual processes. Freehand’s pitch: enterprises spend $16 billion a year on that software and another $348 billion paying people to do what it can’t. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Tariffs, new taxes, and shifting immigration policy are squeezing the outsourcing model further, which is exactly the gap Freehand is chasing.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/qureight-raises-20m-series-b-ai-lung-heart-clinical-trials/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Qureight Raises $20M for AI-powered Lung and Heart Clinical Trials</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">How the Freehand Agents Actually Work</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203832" style="width: 810px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203832" class="size-full wp-image-203832" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Freehand-founders.jpg" alt="A protrait image of the founders of Nitin Jayakrishnan and Abhijeet Manohar in a dual toen background" width="800" height="418" /><p id="caption-attachment-203832" class="wp-caption-text">Freehand Founders</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Freehand was founded in 2024 by Nitin Jayakrishnan and Abhijeet Manohar. Jayakrishnan and Manohar previously built logistics at Pando, where they watched procurement and finance teams lose hours of work to manual assignments. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">That experience shaped their bet: software should replace the work, not just assist with it. The agents run on what Freehand calls a Category Context Graph, blending structured enterprise data with contracts and emails so agents have context before acting. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Instead of suggesting answers like a chatbot, they read supplier contracts, negotiate rates, approve invoices, and reconcile records directly inside enterprise systems. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">“The difference between an agent that acts and a chatbot that suggests is context,” says Manohar. Freehand is competing against well-funded rivals such as Harvey, Norm AI, Abridge, and Writer, who have all raised nine-figure rounds this year as investors chase enterprise AI agents. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">What sets Freehand apart is a narrow focus on procurement and supply-chain finance, plus full production deployments at major companies within roughly two years of founding, not just pilots.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/cor-raises-30m-ai-profitability-agencies-consultancies/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>COR Raises $30M To Boost AI-Driven Profitability</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Results So Far, and What’s Next for Freehand</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">“Freehand marks one of the first full-scale agentic deployments at Unilever and is an early anchor in the shift from software that assists to software that runs our supply chain,” says Matt Algar, Unilever’s global vice president of supply chain.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">According to Grand View Research, the supply-chain management market was about $32.9 billion in 2024. With automation taking over logistics and procurement, it’s on track to more than double to over $76 billion by 2030. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Freehand plans to use the new funding to expand past invoice processing into direct materials and maintenance, repair, and operations spend. This will push to become embedded infrastructure inside supply chains rather than another software layer on top.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">For years, enterprises modernized supply chains by stacking new software on top of outsourced labor. Freehand is betting the next move is removing both at once.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/greyparrot-secures-27-million-series-b-ai-waste-intelligence/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Greyparrot Secures $27M To Scale AI Waste Intelligence Platform</i></b></a></p>
