					<description><![CDATA[<p>Qureight just raised $20 million to fix how to read a chest scan. The Cambridge company builds AI imaging tools for lung and heart clinical trials, and its Series B</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/qureight-raises-20m-series-b-ai-lung-heart-clinical-trials/" data-wpel-link="internal">Qureight Raises $20M for AI-powered Lung and Heart Clinical Trials</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Qureight just raised $20 million to fix how to read a chest scan. The Cambridge company builds AI imaging tools for lung and heart clinical trials, and its Series B was led by </span><a href="https://www.moltenventures.com/news/accelerating-the-future-of-lung-disease-trials-molten-leads-qureights-20m-series-b" data-wpel-link="external" rel="external noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400">Molten Ventures</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">, with backers Hargreave Hale AIM VCT, XTX Ventures, Guinness Ventures, Meltwind, and Ascension all returning.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">From a CT Scan To An AI Company</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203814" style="width: 1034px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203814" class="size-large wp-image-203814" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Team-1024x668.jpg" alt="" width="1024" height="668" /><p id="caption-attachment-203814" class="wp-caption-text">Qureight AI Team</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Without an engineering background, Dr Muhunthan Thillai co-founded Qureight in 2018 with Dr Alessandro Ruggiero. Thillai calls it one of the biggest early hurdles. The idea came from his own work as a chest physician, after a case where he couldn’t confidently interpret a CT scan. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">“There was an area to go and help these pharma companies do better clinical trials, and so that’s how the company started,” he told Tech Funding News. Thillai still sees patients part-time in Cambridge. “It’s very difficult to be a founder and grow a company and still see patients, but I love seeing patients,” he says. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To cover the engineering gap, Qureight hired a CTO who was global head of platform at Hewlett Packard, a CMO who led research at CMR Surgical, and a CSO who used to teach machine learning at Imperial College London.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/cor-raises-30m-ai-profitability-agencies-consultancies/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>COR Raises $30M To Boost AI-Driven Profitability</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Two Products, One Foundation Model</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Qureight runs two products for pharma clients. Workflow cuts imaging decision time from about two weeks to 48 hours. AI Lung models the airways and blood vessels, showing exactly how a drug affects disease progression.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Both sit on a general-purpose foundation model of the chest. The disease-specific model now takes one or two months to build, rather than one year. The funding covers an in-house AI imaging lab. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">It also pushes into asthma, lung cancer, pulmonary hypertension, bronchiectasis, and drug-induced lung toxicity. Qureight currently carries out global trials with AstraZeneca, Bristol Myers Squibb, and several biotech partners.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The lung and heart clinical trials market is projected to hit $27.5 billion by 2030, growing 6.9% a year. Oxford’s Brainomix is the closest European rival. It features an FDA-cleared e-Lung platform used in pulmonary fibrosis trials. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">However, the overlap is smaller than it looks: Brainomix sells diagnostic software to hospitals, while Qureight works on trial design and imaging contract research. The platform was recently picked by Boehringer Ingelheim for a Phase 3 trial. </span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/greyparrot-secures-27-million-series-b-ai-waste-intelligence/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Greyparrot Secures $27M To Scale AI Waste Intelligence Platform</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Why Molten, and What’s Next</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Qureight approached Molten two years ago and got turned down. This time, three lead investors sent term sheets within six weeks, and Qureight could have raised more than it did. It chose Molten anyway, for the relationship and to keep the round anchored to a London fund over competing US offers. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Molten’s healthtech bets include Deciphex and CoachHub, which closed a $200 million round. Dr Inga Deakin, the Molten partner joining Qureight’s board, says: “Qureight demonstrates how AI, powered by real-world data, can accelerate discovery and transform clinical research.”</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Qureight plans to double headcount to 100 by December, open a second London office next month, and get asthma, lung cancer, and pulmonary hypertension trials running before the end of the year. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Whether it becomes the default imaging layer for pharma trials or stays a specialist player depends on what it announces next. Either way, the scan Thillai couldn’t quite read now has three investors fighting to back it.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/hush-security-raises-30m-ai-agent-governance-gap/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Hush Security Raises $30M for Governance AI Agents</i></b></a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/qureight-raises-20m-series-b-ai-lung-heart-clinical-trials/" data-wpel-link="internal">Qureight Raises $20M for AI-powered Lung and Heart Clinical Trials</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
